{
  "fixture": "F41-pli-easytrieve",
  "description": "A customer batch estate in four mainframe languages: a PL/I update program (an %INCLUDE member with the customer record, a file with a TITLE, an ON-unit, SELECT, embedded DB2 SQL and a call to an assembler routine), an Easytrieve report program (FILE layouts, a SORT, a JOB with procedures, a REPORT section, CALL and SQL), a REXX driver (ALLOC and EXECIO of literal datasets, an allocation built at run time, ADDRESS LINKMVS, ISPEXEC SELECT PGM, a queued DSN RUN PROGRAM, INTERPRET and a planted password in a variable) and an assembler date routine (a DCB opened for input, LINK EP=, a V-type constant and LOAD EPLOC=). The commits add a PL/I internal procedure, a second Easytrieve report and a CLIST driver. 'since' names the milestone whose compiler must produce the item. A program is Program {platform: mainframe, name} whatever its language, so the REXX driver's LINKMVS and ISPEXEC calls link to the PL/I and Easytrieve programs and the PL/I CALL to the assembler one.",
